Z||000026||filthyscarecrow||12-18-2001||12:31 AM||||i think it's silly to judge all imports (even all acuras) by what a few people say about one of their models. <BR>i've got a 94 integra and that thing kicks ass. i love it as much as i do my 86SE. (it was built in japan, at least that's what the destination tag says). they're really great cars. i get 30-35 mpg even when i rev to redline, which i do quite often simply because the engine can take it. it sounds awesome. i like it better than the fiero, it has more of a scream to it. i like my cars and my women the same: screamers. <BR>it's had its share of problems too, i had a timing belt break a couple months ago becasue the fokker salesman lied and told me it had been changed. oh well, i lucked out. only cost $50 to fix. <BR>i will not buy another american car unless they build another fiero. but that's just me.||||reg||1
